  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>ENG4_U02_L06_Q01</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p><strong>Question ID:</strong> ENG4_U02_L06_Q01</p><p><strong>MLA Standard:</strong> MLA.ENG4.R.11</p><p>Classic context: In Homer&#39;s The Odyssey, Odysseus spends years trying to return home after war. The epic uses a journey pattern involving obstacles, temptation, disguise, recognition, and the question of what home means after long absence. Contemporary <strong>Passage:</strong> After three years working overseas, Amara landed before dawn in the city where she had grown up. She expected the streets to recognize her, but new towers had risen where the market used to lean into the river. At her mother&#39;s apartment, the lock had been changed for safety, and Amara stood in the hallway with a suitcase and a passport full of stamps. She almost laughed at the old story she had loved as a child, the one where the wanderer returned and the house knew him. Her mother opened the door, studied her face, and said, &quot;You have brought the distance with you.&quot; Only then did Amara understand that coming home was not the end of the journey but the last test of it. Which classic influence is clearest?</p>]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.3333333</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber>ENG4_U02_L06_Q01</idnumber>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>none</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A. A courtroom trial</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>This is not central.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>B. The homecoming journey after long absence</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Correct. Both texts center return and recognition.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>C. A harvest festival</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>This is not present.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>D. A battle scene</p>]]></text>
      <feedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>The modern passage is not about battle.</p>]]></text></feedback>
    </answer>
  </question>
